        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A cheap treadmill lasts longer when it runs cool.</strong> Keep well
            inside the weight and speed ratings, break long sessions up and let the motor rest, lubricate
            the deck on schedule and set the belt tension correctly, and you remove most of the heat and
            friction that end budget motors and boards.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Give it direct, grounded power, a level and clean place to live, and proper storage, and
            register it on day one so the warranty is there when a part does fail. If you are still
            choosing, our guide to the
